domain $R?$\n\n- $R=[-3,3]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[-4,4]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[-3,3]\\times [0,2]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/assets/4a8671db243a19fb258f6144d6aba1b193e237ef93d45d877829f80b93bc7d36.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}9-{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(9-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangle III does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangles I and II cover the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}]}
